{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id16093590"}, "name":{"label":"B_O_O_Y_A_R"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-07-26T04:26:16-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2.3"}, "id":{"label":"1699006414"}, "title":{"label":"Very very good"}, "content":{"label":"Came from Evernote due to bloating and sluggishness\n\nKeep it quick, keep it simple, don't feel you need to add much and I'll keep subscribing", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1016366447&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id335628452"}, "name":{"label":"WorkFlowy student"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-07-13T14:30:21-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2.1"}, "id":{"label":"1681138063"}, "title":{"label":"Bear is a joy to use"}, "content":{"label":"I was looking for a minimal writing app to help me focus while writing my masters thesis and I've found it in bear!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1016366447&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id50014488"}, "name":{"label":"cbpcb"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-07-04T07:18:11-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2.1"}, "id":{"label":"1668586347"}, "title":{"label":"Fantastic. Just a couple of tweaks and would be perfect..."}, "content":{"label":"Bear is an almost perfect app. Once you've figured out the file structure, using hashtags, it's superb, especially for making a cross-referenced library of notes. Being able to use multiple hashtags In a single note means that you can peg an individual note to various 'folders'. Do this across many notes, and a cross-referenced library starts to emerge that reflects the key topics you want to organise it by. If you're doing any academic study, this is a fantastically useful function that you have to have. \n\nThree points for improvement though:\n\n1) Typewriter mode. Holding the cursor at the top of the page, and in the middle (see e.g. Scrivener) would be very useful.\n2) Pinch-and-zoom when in whole-page text view. A thin column of text with large expanses of nothing on either side is a waste of screen.\n3) The drawing mode either needs to give multiple pages (like Notes) or a semi-infinite page (like OneNote). \n\nOtherwise...perfect, especially with the export options of the (relatively cheap) Pro option.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1016366447&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
